*I don't. It's that simple.*

100% Free and Open Source
LMoE is free and will always remain free. There are no Patreon tiers, "buy me a coffee" links, PayPal tip jars, or requests to like and subscribe. 
Crucially, there will never be a "Pro" version that locks features behind a paywall. Whatever is in the main branch is always the latest, most complete, and best version available.

Zero Tracking, Zero Spam
If or when a dedicated website is launched to showcase the hardware build and software documentation, it will be completely ad-free. No sign-up forms, no monthly newsletters, and no collecting your email address.

Complete Data Privacy
LMoE runs entirely on your local machine. Any files or data you "upload" stay strictly on your device and are never transmitted anywhere.

There are three narrow exceptions, all of which are entirely under your control:

Map tiles — In online mode, map tile images are fetched from public government and open-source tile servers (BKG, Esri, OpenStreetMap). 
            These requests contain only the map grid coordinates needed to render the image — no LMoE data, no location, no identifying information. 
            This can be eliminated entirely by configuring a local PMTiles file, after which the map works with zero external contact.

Weather —   If you open the Weather panel, your configured home coordinates (latitude and longitude) are sent to Open-Meteo, a free, open-source, no-account weather API. No other data is transmitted.

Espy sync — When you choose to sync with your Espy field terminal, map data and marker information are sent directly to that device. 
            Espy is an ESP32 CYD you own and control, and its firmware is fully open source and available in this repository.

All other features — including the journal, resource tracker, survival library, supply runs, and LoRa messaging — are entirely local. Nothing leaves your device.

No Paid Dependencies
All third-party services integrated into LMoE are free and/or open source. While some may offer paid tiers, LMoE does not use or require any paid features. 
If you choose not to enter any API keys, those features will fail gracefully and the rest of the application will continue to be fully operational.

I built this for fun, simply to see if I could. I have no interest in charging for it or collecting data about the people who use it.
